Advanced Jenkins Pipelines (Scripted)
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the differences between declarative and scripted Jenkins pipelines
Write and implement scripted Jenkins pipelines using Groovy syntax
Implement advanced logic including conditional statements, loops, and error handling
Use reusable functions and dynamic stage generation in scripted pipelines
Integrate simulated external tool output (quality, security, test reports) into a pipeline workflow
Debug and troubleshoot scripted pipeline issues using the Jenkins console log
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Jenkins and CI/CD concepts
Familiarity with declarative Jenkins pipelines
Basic knowledge of Groovy scripting language
Understanding of Git version control
Linux command line experience
Basic programming concepts (variables, functions, conditionals)
This lab is performed entirely in an isolated, self-owned practice environment (a local or lab-provided Linux virtual machine) for educational purposes. No production systems or external services are touched; all "external tool integration" in this lab is simulated with shell output so the pipeline logic can be studied safely.

